        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/p/b2d939/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2014-12-26T22:07:56.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>sorry if this question is a duplicate, I couldn't find any others like it.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>I was wondering about how aim/dodge tokens stack with attack/defense+1 tokens. &nbsp;Basically, I want to know whether results are increased before or after +1 tokens are applied. If, say, I roll a six with my base dice, can I then spend +1's as auto-6's (assuming they don't auto-miss)? If my highest die on the base roll was a 4 and I spend a +1 and get a 5, do all my base dice improve?&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>I also have a question regarding tokens and multitarget attacks. I get that tokens only apply to one target, but can I distribute multiple tokens among muliple targets? Say I have three attack+1 tokens, and my attack has three targets. &nbsp;Can I spend all my tokens to roll two extra dice against the first target, one against the second, and use only base dice aginst the third? if I have two Aim tokens, can I spend them both on one to improve the dice against two different targets?</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:43:07.340Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "incoming_link_count": 6,
