        "raw": "<p>sorry if this question is a duplicate, I couldn&#39;t find any others like it.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>I was wondering about how aim/dodge tokens stack with attack/defense+1 tokens. &nbsp;Basically, I want to know whether results are increased before or after +1 tokens are applied. If, say, I roll a six with my base dice, can I then spend +1&#39;s as auto-6&#39;s (assuming they don&#39;t auto-miss)? If my highest die on the base roll was a 4 and I spend a +1 and get a 5, do all my base dice improve?&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>I also have a question regarding tokens and multitarget attacks. I get that tokens only apply to one target, but can I distribute multiple tokens among muliple targets? Say I have three attack+1 tokens, and my attack has three targets. &nbsp;Can I spend all my tokens to roll two extra dice against the first target, one against the second, and use only base dice aginst the third? if I have two Aim tokens, can I spend them both on one to improve the dice against two different targets?</p>",
