      {
        "id": 124558,
        "name": "lutherbellhendricksv",
        "username": "lutherbellhendricksv",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/lutherbellhendricksv/{size}/2350_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-12-26T23:32:14.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"payprplayn\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/p/b2d939/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> payprplayn:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>sorry if this question is a duplicate, I couldn't find any others like it.&nbsp;I was wondering about how aim/dodge tokens stack with attack/defense+1 tokens. &nbsp;Basically, I want to know whether results are increased before or after +1 tokens are applied. If, say, I roll a six with my base dice, can I then spend +1's as auto-6's (assuming they don't auto-miss)? If my highest die on the base roll was a 4 and I spend a +1 and get a 5, do all my base dice improve?&nbsp;&nbsp;I also have a question regarding tokens and multitarget attacks. I get that tokens only apply to one target, but can I distribute multiple tokens among muliple targets? Say I have three attack+1 tokens, and my attack has three targets. &nbsp;Can I spend all my tokens to roll two extra dice against the first target, one against the second, and use only base dice aginst the third? if I have two Aim tokens, can I spend them both on one to improve the dice against two different targets?</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Extra dice go into the pool to be affected by Aim or Dodge, just like they were part of the original roll.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>You can divide up Attack tokens between the targets, as you described. You can use multiple Aim tokens to affect multiple targets, if you have a way of getting multiple Aim tokens. (The Aim action is normally Limited, so you'd need a power to give you an Aim token, or something to make the Aim action Unlimited.)</p>",
        "post_number": 2,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:58:36.578Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
